s/OL34740523M/Anglicanism_Methodism_and_Ecumenism","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL34740523M/Anglicanism_Methodism_and_Ecumenism","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2839997A","name":"Andrew Chandler"}],"isbn_13":["9781350155442"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"publish_date":"2020","publishers":["Bloomsbury Publishing Plc"],"source_records":["bwb:9781350155442"],"title":"Anglicanism, Methodism and Ecumenism","weight":"0.286","pagination":"320","subtitle":"A History of the Queen's and Handsworth Colleges","full_title":"Anglicanism, Methodism and Ecumenism A History of the Queen's and Handsworth Colleges","works":[{"key":"/works/OL21341344W"}],"key":"/books/OL34740523M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-10-07T16:00:46.733210"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-10-07T16:00:46.733210"}}},"ISBN:9781788312790":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781788312790","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28905634M/Anglicanism_Methodism_and_Ecumenism","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28905634M/Anglicanism_Methodism_and_Ecumenism","details":{"publishers":["I. B. Tauris & Company, Limited"],"subtitle":"A History of Queen's and Handsworth Colleges","source_records":["bwb:9781788312790","marc:marc_bloomsbury/2025MAR_bloomsbury.mrc:31554160:5142"],"title":"Anglicanism, Methodism and Ecumenism","number_of_pages":320,"isbn_13":["9781788312790"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lc_classifications":["BV4160","BV4140.G7 C43 2018eb"],"publish_date":"2018","key":"/books/OL28905634M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2839997A","name":"Andrew Chandler"}],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL21341344W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["Church of england, clergy","Methodist church, clergy"],"oclc_numbers":["1128166983"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"For almost 200 years, the city of Birmingham has been a key location for the training of clergy. From 1828 Anglican clergy studied at the Queen's College and in 1881 the Methodist Church developed their own training facility at Handsworth College. In this book, Andrew Chandler tells the tale of these two colleges. This is a history not simply of the creation and evolution of these two religious institutions, but a study full of significance for the wider history of Christianity in British society across the nineteenth and twentieth centuries. The foundation of both colleges occurred in a confident age of civic progress and reform and their subsequent histories reveal much that was at work in the experience of the British churches at large. They were at first expressions of denominational identity and a determination to educate a class of clergy. In time they found themselves negotiating new prospects within the ecumenical currents of a later age and the deepening realities of secularization. In 1970 they united. This is a book which blends local, national and international dimensions and also shows how the two theological colleges came to embrace all kinds of intellectual, cultural, social and political history in a period of restless change.\"--"},"identifiers":{"doi":["10.5040/9781350985315"]},"latest_revision":2,"revision":2,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-17T18:07:15.037379"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-04-30T10:02:31.111482"}}},"ISBN:9781838607999":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781838607999","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL34739349M/Anglicanism_Methodism_and_Ecumenism","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL34739349M/Anglicanism_Methodism_and_Ecumenism","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2839997A","name":"Andrew Chandler"}],"isbn_13":["9781838607999"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"publish_date":"2018","publishers":["I. B. Tauris & Company, Limited"],"source_records":["bwb:9781838607999"],"title":"Anglicanism